<title>GERMANY: Meister-cannot imagine EMU without France, Germany.</title>
<headline>Meister-cannot imagine EMU without France, Germany.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank directorate member Edgar Meister said on Monday that he could not imagine European currency union starting without Germany and France as member nations.</p>
<p>&quot;I personally can only imagine currency union with both countries. I cannot imagine EMU without France or Germany,&quot; Meister told journalists at a ceremony to hand over the presidency of the European Monetary Institute.</p>
<p>Bundesbank officials have said repeatedly that a currency union without Europe's two largest nations would make little sense.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
